From: Squeezebox RG35XX-H project (WP3 panel bring-up)
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] pwm: sun4i: bind the H616 PWM block with H6 driver data
Upstream-Status: Pending (H616 PWM DT binding not yet upstreamed; IP block
 matches H6: 2 channels, prescaler bypass, direct mod-clock output)
Squeezebox-OOT: yes - required for pwm-backlight brightness control

The H616 PWM controller (0x0300a000) is the same IP as the H6 PWM
block. Add the allwinner,sun50i-h616-pwm compatible reusing the H6
driver data so the RG35XX-H panel backlight (PWM0 on PD28) can be
driven with brightness control instead of a GPIO on/off interim.

Validation: DTB build + pwm-sun4i cross-compile clean. Backlight
polarity/period must be confirmed on hardware (see
device-tree/BRINGUP_PANEL.md); falls back to gpio-backlight if PWM
proves wrong.

--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-sun4i.c
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-sun4i.c
@@ -368,6 +368,9 @@
 		.compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h6-pwm",
 		.data = &sun50i_h6_pwm_data,
 	}, {
+		.compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-pwm",
+		.data = &sun50i_h6_pwm_data,
+	}, {
 		/* sentinel */
 	}
 };
